.TH QUALITY-MANAGER 1 "November 2026" "quality_manager 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quality-manager \- coordinate autonomous Ada quality workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quality-manager
.RI [ --config " PATH" ]
.RI [ --format " terminal|json|markdown" ]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quality Manager persists maintenance, campaign, and release-qualification state
while preserving the measurement, planning, approval, and execution authority of
its upstream systems.
.SH INSPECTION COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Validate configuration and negotiate the model_runner headless contract.
.TP
.B status, queue, approvals, history, events, recover
Read durable coordinator state. JSON output uses schema version 1. The recover
view reports journal state for manual reconciliation; it does not blindly repeat
an ambiguous external operation.
.SH WORKFLOW COMMANDS
.TP
.B maintenance [--project ID|PATH] [--dry-run]
Run one restart-safe maintenance cycle.
.TP
.B daemon [--once] [--project ID|PATH] [--dry-run]
Run continuous maintenance or one daemon iteration.
.TP
.B campaign-create DEFINITION
Create an immutable campaign definition revision.
.TP
.B campaign-start|campaign-pause|campaign-resume|campaign-reconcile ID
Control a persisted campaign.
.TP
.B release-create PROJECT PROFILE
Create an immutable release candidate.
.TP
.B release-qualify ID
Qualify only when current assessment and release-check evidence is available.
.TP
.B release-export ID OUTPUT
Verify and export a qualified evidence bundle.
.SH AUTHORIZATION
.TP
.B approve RECORD | reject RECORD
Import an exact JSON decision conforming to approval-decision-v1.schema.json.
The command must match the decision in the record. Decisions are append-only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates the requested operation completed. A negative quality result,
missing evidence, incompatible contract, authorization requirement, or execution
failure returns nonzero and retains its diagnostic evidence.
.SH FILES
.I config/quality-manager.toml
is the default configuration. Generated coordinator databases and reports must
not be committed.
